 696            /
 697            /       HERE BEGINS THE DISPLAY CALCULATIONS FOR THE TWO SHIPS.  AT
 698            /       THIS POINT ONLY THE POSITION AND ORIENTATION OF EACH VESSEL
 699            /       IS ONF INTEREST SINCE THE VELOCITY AND ALL THAT HAVE ALREADY
 700            /       BEEN TAKEN CARE OF.  FOR THE BOTH SHIPS THE DISPLAY FILES ARE
 701            /       CALCULATED AS A SERIES OF PAIRS OF X,Y COORDINATES.  BETWEEN
 702            /       EACH PAIR OF POINTS A FOUR POINT VECTOR WILL BE DRAWN.  THE
 703            /       ACTUAL COORDINATES ARE CALCULATED AS DISPLACEMENTS
 704            /       FROM THE CENTRAL PSOTION OF THE SHIP, TAKING INTO ACCOUNT THE
 705            /       ANGLE OF ORIENTATION.  THE FORMULAS FOLLOWED ARE:
 706            /
 707            /       X(POINT)=X(BASE)+X(REL)*COS[THE]+Y(REL)*SINE[THE]
 708            /
 709            /       Y(POINT)=Y(BASE)+Y(REL)*COS[THE]-X(REL)*SINE[THE]
 710            /
 711            /       WHERE SINE[THE] AND COS[THE] ARE THE FUNCTIONS OF THE
 712            /       ANGLE OF ORIENTATION, X(BASE) AND Y(BASE) ARE THE 
 713            /       COORDINATES OF THE SHIPS POSITION AND X(REL) AND Y(REL)
 714            /       CORRESPOND TO DISPLACEMENT PAIRS DEPENDING ON THE SHAPE
 715            /       OF THE FIGURE.  ALL X AND Y RELS LIE WITHIN THE RANGE 0-3 AND
 716            /       THERE FORE ALL NECESSARY DISPLACEMENTS FROM BASE COORDINATES
 717            /       MAY BE CALCULATEDFROM DIFFERENT COMBINATIONS OF T10SIN, T20COS
 718            /       ETC.  THESE VALUES ARE CALCULATED BY A CALL TO POSCAL WITH THE SINE 
 719            /       AND COSINE OF THE ANGLE OF INTEREST IN CALSIN AND CALCOS.
 720            /
 721            /       FOLLOWING THIS METHOD ANY FIGURE DESCRIBABLE WITH A 7 BY 7
 722            /       MATRIX OF POINTS MAY BE QUICKLY CALCULATED.
 723            /
 724            /       BEGINNING AT ONESET DIFFERENT DISPLACEMENT PAIRS ARE CALCULATED
 725            /       AND DEPOSITIED THROUGH AUTO10 TO FORM THE DISPLAY FILE FOR SHIP NUMBER ONE.
 726            /
 727            
